", "Open seat with Walz not on the ballot removes an incumbency advantage", "Prediction markets and most expert ratings still strongly favor Democrats"], "rationale": "The polling average sits near nine points for Klobuchar, but the newest surveys, including a Republican-sponsored poll showing just a two-point race, point to tightening, so the forecast moves modestly below the combined ten-point baseline. Klobuchar's roughly twenty-to-one fundraising advantage and consistently strong ratings keep her clearly favored despite the open seat.", "watch": "The upcoming televised debates and Demuth's outside PAC spending could further narrow the gap if Klobuchar stumbles or the tightening trend continues.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Tim Walz (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Minnesota's governorship is open with Tim Walz retiring, and Senator Amy Klobuchar enters the general election as a clear favorite over state Representative Lisa Demuth. Polls through mid-September show Klobuchar leading by margins ranging from two to ten points, with the most recent surveys suggesting the race has tightened from earlier double-digit spreads. Klobuchar has raised over seven million dollars to Demuth's roughly four hundred thousand, though Demuth has benefited from outside PAC support.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9683, "margin": 10.03}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9347, "margin": 8.5}]}